If gamma and epsilon are to be set to zero, then under that model the two years are independent (with possibly different detection probabilities).  You could then simply feed occu the data as if you had twice the sample size (each season providing a "separate" set of sites).  You'd get the estimates and an AIC value for comparison purposes to an unrestricted model fit in colext.  Or am I misunderstanding the estimation issue?

