Hi all,

I'm curious if there has been any progress on this topic and if there is a better way to manually fix parameters in the current version of pcountOpen in unmarked. I'm working with a data set of tropical migrants wintering in Belize and we are having trouble getting reasonable estimates of survival in an open model likely because of erratic survey frequency (i.e., lots of NAs). We were thinking that we could input estimates of seasonal survival from near-by mark-recapture efforts in order to get a better overall estimates of abundance for target species. First off, if this a terrible idea for whatever reason please let me know. If it isn't a terrible idea, is there a good way to implement it in unmarked or should I move toward another programming option like BUGS?

