Andy,

Thanks for your response.  I wanted to followup with a couple of additional questions.

1) I constructed the data frame, used the summary function, and fit the model with the code given below. Does it look like the "sample size" is large enough?  Even when I get convergence, it takes a very long time when using optim  (is there lots of looping going on?)  I find the half-normal distance function to be especially difficult to get convergence.

umf<-unmarkedFrameGDSy=y,yearlySiteCovs=vars,numPrimary=2,dist.breaks=c(0,50,100),survey="point",unitsIn="m")
summary(umf)

unmarkedFrame Object

