Rhetoric on incremental improvement doesn't seem to get us very far without some measure of what has improved. I was making a serious point in my last post: why sweat the small assumptions if you ignore the big ones and only care about robustness? I'm all for pragmatism and a focus on robustness, but let's see that demonstrated rather than just claimed. Of course the answer lies in spatially explicit analysis using additional data to estimate the spatial scale of detection - why didn't I think of that?
Murray

