1) When modeling the probability of detection, the researchers I am working with are interesting in using time (time of day) as a covariate.  I have seen this done before by other researchers using unmarked, but I question if it makes sense to believe that the relationship between time and the probability of detection would be linear.  Is it typical to use time as a continuous covariate in these types of models?

